<header class="nav">
  <div class="brand">
    zoption
    <span class="brand-sub">NIFTY option selling</span>
  </div>
  <!-- Three links on purpose. The scalper's and the Price-Filter engine's pages
       still EXIST and still work — /, /pfe, /trades, /events and /settings are
       unchanged — they are simply not advertised here, because this deployment
       runs the Option Selling Engine and a nav offering three engines invites
       an operator to configure the one that is not running.

       The OSE's own settings live at /ose/settings, linked from the /ose page,
       so removing the global Settings link does not strand anything. -->
  <nav>
    <a href="/ose"       class="<%= page === 'ose'       ? 'on' : '' %>">Option Selling</a>
    <a href="/terminal"  class="<%= page === 'terminal'  ? 'on' : '' %>">Terminal</a>
    <a href="/brokers"   class="<%= page === 'brokers'   ? 'on' : '' %>">Broker</a>
  </nav>
  <form method="post" action="/logout" class="logout">
    <button type="submit" class="link">Sign out</button>
  </form>
</header>
